<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/06af6c2479be> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Audit Report on the New York City Police Department’s Oversight of Its Agreement with ShotSpotter Inc. for the Gunshot Detection and Location System" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3843" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/11b912c0c5db> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Last September, the Durham school board voted to prohibit ShotSpotter from installing its sensors on school campuses." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2626" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/279b7fdd4039> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[3844] ShotSpotter, a system the Police Department uses to detect gunfire, is overwhelmingly inaccurate and leads officers to spend hundreds of hours each month investigating nonexistent shots, according to an audit the New York City comptroller released Thursday." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3844" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3d0ad19a5e36> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[3843] In July 2019, at the request of ShotSpotter, The Policing Project at NYU Law School conducted a Privacy Audit and Assessment of ShotSpotter, Inc.'s Gunshot Detection Technology." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3843" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/45894ee52a48> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Troy will turn off ShotSpotter" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "1247" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/47b11d2cfb95> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "ShotSpotter technology has been available for only two weeks in parts of Durham -- but didn't activate during a mass shooting over the weekend." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2309" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/4c0bb399712e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The shooting on North Miami Boulevard occurred within the area the ShotSpotter technology is supposed to detect gun shots." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2309" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5dc3cf9ffbb9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In Boston, the mayor and the police department are on the defensive after three members of the state's congressional delegation signed a letter that called for a national probe into the system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3844" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6c2d9dc8a739> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[3843] ...uses acoustic sensors to detect gunshot activity to assist the NYPD in pinpointing the location of suspected gunfire within areas covered by the system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3843" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/791c120b8534> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Gunshot Detection System Wastes N.Y.P.D. Officers’ Time, Audit Finds" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3844" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/791f79a9a75a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[2473] The Durham Police Department hopes ShotSpotter will help officers quickly respond to gunfire." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2473" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7c246a564be7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Durham County began its one-year pilot of ShotSpotter last December." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2626" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/960ad7a2a7ec> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[3844] New York must decide before December whether to renew its contract with SoundThinking, the California company that owns the system, and the audit advises officials to decline until the system can be fully evaluated." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3844" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/98661bf15627> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Controversial ShotSpotter gunshot detection technology failed to pick up two recent deadly shootings in Durham" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2626" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9b107f379d15> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Copyright 2023 Nexstar Media Inc. All rights reserved." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2473" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b257d76f7ff2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[3844] ShotSpotter, a system the Police Department uses to detect gunfire, is overwhelmingly inaccurate..." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3844" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c12d419e208c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[3844] ShotSpotter, a system the Police Department uses to detect gunfire, is overwhelmingly inaccurate and leads officers to spend hundreds of hours each month investigating nonexistent shots, according to an audit the New York City comptroller released Thursday." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3844" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c2002832be1c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In its contract with the city, ShotSpotter commits to detecting and locating 90% of unsuppressed outdoor gunfire when the fired rounds are above .25 caliber." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2626" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c383050d4063> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The ShotSpotter System (ShotSpotter) is a Gunshot Detection and Location System (GDLS) that uses acoustic sensors to detect gunshot activity to assist the NYPD in pinpointing the location of suspected gunfire within areas covered by the system." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "3843" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c5430bf5f455> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Middleton says there may a good reason the gunfire detection technology did not notify police." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "2309" .

